  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 61. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 実例 — 実際にあった例。\n2. 自動化 — 人が操作しなくても機械などが行うようにすること。\n3. 自筆 — 自分の手で書くことやその文字。\n4. 時報 — 今の時刻を知らせる音や放送。\n5. 事務所 — 書類や連絡などの仕事をする場所。\n6. ジャッジ — 競技などの審判や判定。\n7. ジャンル — 作品などを内容や形式で分けた種類。\n8. 獣医 — 動物の病気やけがを診る医師。\n9. 十字 — 縦と横の線が交わった形。\n10. 熟語 — 複数の漢字などが結びついてできた言葉。\n11. 受講 — 講義や授業を受けること。\n12. 樹脂 — 木から出るやにのなかまやそれに似た性質の材料。\n13. ジュニア — 年下の人や年少の選手などを表す呼び方。\n14. 樹皮 — 木の幹などの外側を覆う皮。\n15. 樹木 — 幹や枝を持つ木。\n16. 授与 — 賞や証書などを与えること。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
